{"availability":"available","full":"robokrunch/awesome-jev","name":"awesome-jev","description":"A curated list of resources for Jev — TypeSafe AI's System One decision model. Maintained by RoboKrunch.","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"stars":2,"forks":3,"created":"2026-09-19T23:11:42Z","updated":"2026-10-08T19:26:40Z","license":"CC0-1.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://robokrunch.com","topics":["ai-agents","awesome-list","edge-ai","jev","robotics","typesafe"],"demo":"https://preporato.com/jev","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:36.957Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:36.957Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:07:36.957Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:17:21.294Z","stars":3,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:29:27.793Z","stars":2,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:07:36.957Z","stars":2,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A curated list of resources for Jev — TypeSafe AI's \"System One\" model that returns typed, calibrated decisions instead of text.","Jev doesn't chat. You send it structured state; it returns a probability distribution over your predefined options in 70–500ms, at $0.042 per million input tokens with output free. It was built by Diogo Almeida (ex-OpenAI, co-inventor of RLHF/ChatGPT), emerged from stealth in September 2026 with $40M in funding, and went generally available on 2026-09-21: no waitlist, $5 starter credits (120M tokens), with Vercel, Cloudflare, LangChain and Langfuse already adding it to their stacks (per Indian Express).","This list is maintained by RoboKrunch — we benchmark Chinese edge-AI hardware and run our own real-measurement Jev experiments (300 real API calls, real latency, real bills). Entries with our own measured numbers are marked 📊."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"6af42a5140e8f04c1ea0c5fe64fff0d04a0524ece90bebb03f5e598229d7860a","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:48.603Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:48.603Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A curated list of resources for Jev — TypeSafe AI's \"System One\" model that returns typed, calibrated decisions instead of text.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"kouhxp/gutsy — Open local decision models with calibrated probabilities: gutsy-0.8b v0.3 is a Qwen3.5-0.8B fine-tune behind a Jev-style Decisions-format API (yes/no, choice, score), so existing System One clients need only a new base URL — no text generation, no network calls, no per-call cost. (2★, Apache-2.0, created 2026-10-01; real non-fork verified via GitHub API, raw…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"required","text":"taifoon-io/jev — @taifoon/jev: a grader for agent jobs — \"did the AI agent do the work it was paid for?\" Code checks the facts, Jev answers four closed questions about the delivery, and code turns the answers into complete / reject / needs-review with a receipt anyone can recompute. (0★, TypeScript, created 2026-09-27; real non-fork verified via GitHub API, raw README verified)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Explicitly not an OpenAI/TypeSafe/OpenRouter product; generation still runs on your Codex login. (1★, no license declared, created 2026-09-29; real non-fork verified via GitHub API, raw README verified)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"Install from source for now; needs a TypeSafe API key. (0★, Apache-2.0, created 2026-09-29; real non-fork verified via GitHub API, raw README verified)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Author reports 300–550 ms and 20–120 elements per decision on TypeSafe direct (11K input tokens ≈ $0.0005/step); guarded targets (pay/delete/upload/confirm, EN + 中文), login pages, free text and low-confidence steps escalate to a human.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"gherardo200-glitch/jev-bouncer — Self-hosted Telegram moderation bot: Jev scores scam/spam/toxicity per message instead of one open-ended LLM call per message, and thresholds decide warn/delete/mute/ban/flag; npm run demo runs eight realistic sample messages through the exact decision engine with zero keys and zero network (a deterministic local heuristic stands in for the Jev…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"6af42a5140e8f04c1ea0c5fe64fff0d04a0524ece90bebb03f5e598229d7860a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:48.606Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T19:24:38Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/robokrunch/awesome-jev/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T02:55:48.621Z","hash":"6af42a5140e8f04c1ea0c5fe64fff0d04a0524ece90bebb03f5e598229d7860a","originalBytes":639219,"storedBytes":639219,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["jev","verified","api","real","via","created","github","readme","raw","non-fork","mit","typesafe","one","model","decision","python","code","license","declared","agent","per","decisions","typed","author","own","local","against","questions","claude","live","every","typescript","choice","llm","score","benchmark","run","system","models","only","confidence","plus","question","text","independent","each","runs","demo","same","cost","answers","accuracy","repo","latency","full","tool","open","routing","ships","noul","openrouter","data","never","request","through","calibration","key","agents","apache